  "note": "Annual retirement of two councillors in each of the five wards of Londonderry Corporation; nominations Monday 5 January, poll Thursday 15 January 1931. Only the South Ward was contested, where the retiring Labour councillor Francis Callaghan was opposed by two nominees of the Nationalist Association (Derry Journal, 7, 16 and 19 January 1931). 'do.' (ditto) = Nationalist as printed. The other retiring councillor, Hugh Kelly (Labour), did not seek re-election."
